{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782351310928,"sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"bash_57","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e \"import('./dist/data.js').then(({loadDataset}) => { const d = loadDataset(); const atletico = d.matches.filter(m => m.season === 2019 && m.competition === 'Brasileirão' && (m.homeTeam.toLowerCase().includes('atletico') || m.awayTeam.toLowerCase().includes('atletico'))); const names = new Set(); atletico.forEach(m => { names.add(m.homeTeam); names.add(m.awayTeam); }); console.log([...names].sort()); })\"","description":"Finds Atletico team names in 2019"},"output":"[\n  'Athletico-PR',     'Atletico',\n  'Atletico-MG',      'Avai',\n  'Bahia',            'Botafogo',\n  'Botafogo RJ',      'Ceara',\n  'Chapecoense',      'Corinthians',\n  'Cruzeiro',         'Csa',\n  'EC Bahia',         'Flamengo',\n  'Fluminense',       'Fortaleza',\n  'Fortaleza FC',     'Goias',\n  'Gremio',           'Internacional',\n  'Palmeiras',        'Santos',\n  'Sao Paulo',        'Vasco',\n  'Vasco Da Gama RJ'\n]\n","metadata":{"output":"[\n  'Athletico-PR',     'Atletico',\n  'Atletico-MG',      'Avai',\n  'Bahia',            'Botafogo',\n  'Botafogo RJ',      'Ceara',\n  'Chapecoense',      'Corinthians',\n  'Cruzeiro',         'Csa',\n  'EC Bahia',         'Flamengo',\n  'Fluminense',       'Fortaleza',\n  'Fortaleza FC',     'Goias',\n  'Gremio',           'Internacional',\n  'Palmeiras',        'Santos',\n  'Sao Paulo',        'Vasco',\n  'Vasco Da Gama RJ'\n]\n","exit":0,"description":"Finds Atletico team names in 2019","truncated":false},"title":"Finds Atletico team names in 2019","time":{"start":1782351310915,"end":1782351310926}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Still inflated - \"Atletico\" appears with 112 pts and 26 losses, which suggests there are multiple \"Atletico\" teams being merged (Atletico-MG, Atletico-PR, Atletico-GO). My normalization maps \"Atlético Mineiro\" to \"Atletico-MG\" but leaves \"Atlético-PR\" as \"Athletico-PR\". However, some raw data may just say \"Atlético\" or \"Atletico\" which normalizes to \"Atletico\". This is a team name normalization issue.\n\nI should improve normalization to not collapse different Atletico teams. But the raw data in some files just says \"Atletico-PR\" vs \"Atletico-MG\". Let me check what's in the data. The issue is likely \"Athletico-PR\" vs \"Atletico Paranaense\" etc.\n\nActually, the standings show \"Atletico\" with 112 pts. This could be because some source uses \"Atletico\" without suffix, and my normalize keeps it as \"Atletico\". I should make the mapping more specific. For teams with \"Atletico\" + state, keep them separate. For generic \"Atletico\", maybe leave as-is.\n\nBut the bigger issue: even after deduplication, 2019 Brasileirão has 53 matches? Wait, 41+7+5 = 53 for Flamengo, which is correct for a 38-match season plus cup? No, 53 is too many. It might be because the extended dataset has \"Brasileirao\" data plus the main Brasileirao_Matches. Deduplication by date+home+away+competition should handle that, unless team names differ between sources (e.g., \"Athletico-PR\" vs \"Athletico Paranaense\" -> teamKey differs). \n\nThe spec examples show realistic point totals (Flamengo 90 pts for 2019). My 130 pts indicates remaining duplication. The deduplication isn't catching all duplicates because team name normalization differs between sources.\n\nThis is a significant issue. Let me improve:\n1. Better team name normalization so that \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"Atletico Paranaense\", \"Athletico Paranaense\" all map to the same key.\n2. Maybe deduplicate also by season+round+home+away+competition if date is missing or differs.\n\nActually the best approach: the main Brasileirao_Matches.csv and novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv overlap for years 2012-2019. For those years, we should prefer one source. The extended dataset has different tournaments. Let me check the years covered by each.\n\nBrasileirao_Matches.csv: starts 2012. novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv: 2003-2019. They overlap 2012-2019. BR-Football-Dataset: has various tournaments including \"Brasileirao\" probably recent years.\n\nI could deduplicate more aggressively by normalizing the match key to use teamKey which handles name variations. But the problem is some variations aren't mapping. Let me improve teamKey/normalizeTeamName to handle \"Atletico\" better.\n\nActually, I think the issue is \"Atletico\" appearing as a separate team from \"Atletico-MG\". Let me check the raw team names in the datasets for 2019.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6aa33a001PaqcwY05wC6EII","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","messageID":"msg_efc6a594a001GRBu2atEz3PXxV"}}
