s\",\n+    \"esporte clube bahia\": \"Bahia\",\n+    \"fortaleza esporte clube\": \"Fortaleza\",\n+    \"ceará sporting club\": \"Ceara\",\n+    \"avaí futebol clube\": \"Avai\",\n+    \"goiás esporte clube\": \"Goias\",\n+    \"atlético goianiense\": \"Atletico-GO\",\n+    \"atletico goianiense\": \"Atletico-GO\",\n+    \"red bull bragantino\": \"Bragantino\",\n+    \"clube athletico paranaense\": \"Athletico-PR\",\n+    \"athletico paranaense\": \"Athletico-PR\",\n+    \"atlético paranaense\": \"Athletico-PR\",\n+    \"atletico paranaense\": \"Athletico-PR\",\n+    \"cuiabá esporte clube\": \"Cuiaba\",\n+    \"boavista sport club\": \"Boavista\",\n+    \"américa futebol clube\": \"America-MG\",\n+    \"américa - mg\": \"America-MG\",\n+    \"america - mg\": \"America-MG\",\n+    \"centro sportivo alagoano\": \"CSA\",\n+    \"paysandu sport club\": \"Paysandu\",\n+    \"ponte preta\": \"Ponte Preta\",\n+    \"ec bahia\": \"Bahia\",\n+    \"fortaleza fc\": \"Fortaleza\",\n+    \"botafogo rj\": \"Botafogo\",\n+    \"vasco da gama rj\": \"Vasco\",\n+  };\n+\n+  if (fullMappings[lowerPre]) {\n+    return fullMappings[lowerPre];\n+  }\n+\n+  // Remove state suffixes like -SP, -RJ, -MG, -PR, -RS, etc.\n+  // But preserve suffixes that are required to distinguish clubs.\n+  const stateMatch = normalized.match(/-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$/);\n+  if (stateMatch) {\n+    const withoutState = normalized.replace(/-\\s*[A-Z]{2}$/, \"\").trim();\n+    const base = withoutState.toLowerCase();\n+    const ambiguousBases = new Set([\n+      \"atletico\",\n+      \"athletico\",\n+      \"america\",\n+      \"america-mg\",\n+      \"athletico-pr\",\n+    ]);\n+    if (!ambiguousBases.has(base)) {\n+      normalized = withoutState;\n+    }\n+  }\n+\n   normalized = normalized.trim();\n \n-  // Common full-name mappings\n+  // Short-form mappings after suffix handling\n   const lower = normalized.toLowerCase();\n   const mappings: Record<string, string> = {\n     \"sport club corinthians paulista\": \"Corinthians\",\n     \"sao paulo fc\": \"Sao Paulo\",\n","additions":72,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"src/normalize.ts","time":{"start":1782351368121,"end":1782351368124}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Both Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR collapse to \"Atletico\" because my normalizeTeamName strips the state suffix from \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" resulting in \"Atletico\". That's a bug! I shouldn't strip state suffixes from team names that have them as part of the canonical name. \n\nThe issue is my state suffix regex is too aggressive. It strips \"-SP\", \"-MG\", \"-PR\", etc. from all team names. But \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" need to keep their state suffix to distinguish them.\n\nFor the main datasets, Brasileirao_Matches.csv uses \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\" etc., and we want to normalize those to \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\" because they're unique without state. But for \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\", we want to keep them distinct.\n\nSolution: Only strip state suffix if it doesn't create ambiguity. Or, better, after stripping state suffix, check if the result is ambiguous (e.g., \"Atletico\") and if so, keep the original or map to a canonical with state.\n\nA simpler approach: don't strip state suffix blindly. Instead, map full names including state suffixes. Or keep the state suffix for teams where it's part of the identity.\n\nActually, the spec says to normalize team names for consistent matching. The key is consistent matching, not necessarily removing all suffixes. So for \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\", we should keep the state suffix.\n\nLet me change the approach: instead of stripping all state suffixes, only strip them for teams that have a known mapping without suffix. Or, process mappings BEFORE stripping state suffix.\n\nActually, the cleanest approach: \n1. Apply full-name mappings first.\n2. Then strip state suffix only if the resulting name isn't ambiguous.\n\nBut we don't know all ambiguous names. Alternatively, we can keep the state suffix for any name containing \"Atletico\" or \"Athletico\". \n\nLet me think about this more. The state suffix is useful for distinguishing:\n- Atletico-MG vs Atletico-PR\n- Athletico-PR vs others\n\nBut for Palmeiras-SP, Flamengo-RJ, Corinthians-SP, etc., the state suffix is redundant.\n\nI could maintain a list of \"ambiguous\" base names that should keep state suffix. Or I could strip the state suffix but then re-add it for Atletico teams.\n\nSimplest fix: in normalizeTeamName, after stripping state suffix, check if the result is \"atletico\" (case-insensitive), and if so keep the original name (or the version with state). Similarly for \"athletico\".\n\nActually, a better approach: after stripping state suffix, if result.toLowerCase() is in {\"atletico\", \"athletico\"}, restore the state suffix. Let me implement that.\n\nBut wait, what about \"America-MG\"? The state suffix distinguishes America-MG from America-RJ. So I should be more general. But for now, Atletico is the main issue.\n\nAlso, I should handle \"Botafogo RJ\" -> \"Botafogo\", \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" -> \"Vasco\", \"EC Bahia\" -> \"Bahia\", \"Fortaleza FC\" -> \"Fortaleza\", \"CSA\" normalization.\n\nLet me improve normalizeTeamName.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6b2f00001lINqU2SJqjJCZT","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","messageID":"msg_efc6ae7a5001XZ6t2cMBDpcs6r"}}
