-PR\". Good.\n\nWait, \"Athletico-PR\" lower is \"athletico-pr\". The second mappings block doesn't have that key. But it has \"clube athletico paranaense\" -> \"Athletico-PR\". So if input is \"Clube Athletico Paranaense\", fullMappings returns \"Athletico-PR\". If input is \"Athletico-PR\", it stays. Good.\n\nFor \"America-MG\": fullMappings has \"américa futebol clube\" -> \"America-MG\", \"américa - mg\" -> \"America-MG\". But \"America-MG\" itself: lowerPre \"america-mg\" not in fullMappings, state suffix - base \"america\" is ambiguous, so preserved -> \"America-MG\". Then second block lower \"america-mg\" not in mappings. So it stays \"America-MG\". Good.\n\nFor \"Atletico-PR\" (from raw data): stays \"Atletico-PR\" or becomes \"Athletico-PR\"? Wait, the raw data might have \"Atletico-PR\" (not Athletico). Let me check. In 2019 list, I saw \"Athletico-PR\" as normalized. But raw might be \"Athletico-PR\" already. Let me not worry.\n\nThe duplicate mappings are messy but functional. Let me clean it up by removing the second block entirely and just doing a final trim. The first block handles full names, and state suffix stripping handles the rest.\n\nWait, but for \"Palmeiras\" -> lowerPre \"palmeiras\" not in fullMappings, state suffix stripped (no state), returns \"Palmeiras\". Good. For \"Flamengo\" -> returns \"Flamengo\". For \"Sao Paulo\" -> fullMappings? No, fullMappings has \"sao paulo fc\" but not \"sao paulo\". So \"Sao Paulo\" -> state suffix stripped (none) -> lower \"sao paulo\" not in fullMappings, then if we remove second block, returns \"Sao Paulo\". Good.\n\nActually, the second block is mostly redundant because the first block handles full names. But there are cases like \"Flamengo\" -> already fine. \"Gremio\" -> fullMappings has \"grêmio foot-ball portoalegrense\" and \"gremio foot-ball portoalegrense\" but not \"gremio\". So \"Gremio\" stays \"Gremio\" - fine.\n\nI think I can remove the second mappings block. But I need to make sure \"São Paulo\" without FC maps to \"Sao Paulo\" (no accent). The fullMappings has \"são paulo fc\" but not \"são paulo\". After removing second block, \"São Paulo\" would normalize to \"São Paulo\" with accent, then teamKey removes accent. But the displayed name would be \"São Paulo\" while other sources display \"Sao Paulo\". That's inconsistent. So I should add \"são paulo\" and \"sao paulo\" to fullMappings.\n\nSimilarly, \"Grêmio\" should map to \"Gremio\", \"Atlético-MG\" should map to \"Atletico-MG\" (accent), etc.\n\nLet me just clean up the second block and add the short-form mappings to fullMappings. Or keep both blocks but make them cleaner.\n\nActually, the simplest thing: keep the second block but make it only for short forms. But the current second block duplicates many full names. Let me remove duplicates and keep only short forms in second block. Or just remove second block entirely and rely on first block + state suffix handling.\n\nLet me do a clean refactor: remove second block, add needed short forms to first block.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6c106a001ZYl9vFh2dYwwTw","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","messageID":"msg_efc6ba3ec001EKFtXLH6FIVYMH"}}
