uter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The extended dataset has Brasileirão matches from 2014-2023, but the main Brasileirao_Matches.csv covers 2012-2023. There's overlap. The extra 7 Flamengo matches in 2019 have weird dates that don't match the main dataset. These are probably from a different source/league or have date issues. But they're labeled \"Brasileirao\" in the raw data.\n\nTo avoid double-counting, I should improve deduplication. One approach: deduplicate by season+home+away+competition, keeping the first source. This would ensure each fixture pair appears once per season. But in a double-round-robin league, teams play twice per season (home and away), so season+home+away would collapse both matches. Not good.\n\nBetter: deduplicate by date+home+away+competition but also handle date mismatches by checking if there's a match within a few days with the same teams and same competition. But that could incorrectly collapse legitimate close matches.\n\nAlternative: source preference. For each competition, define a preferred source order. For Brasileirão, prefer Brasileirao_Matches.csv and novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv over BR-Football-Dataset.csv. This is clean.\n\nActually, the simplest fix: in the deduplication, prefer sources in the order they are loaded, and we already load Brasileirao first, then Cup, Libertadores, then Extended, then Historical. So Extended matches should be skipped if a duplicate exists from an earlier source. The issue is the date differs, so they're not considered duplicates.\n\nMaybe I should change the deduplication key to ignore exact date and use season+round+home+away+competition for round-robin leagues? But round info differs between sources.\n\nHmm. For the demo, 109 pts vs 90 pts is not ideal but acceptable. The spec example shows 90 pts. Let me see if I can get closer.\n\nActually, I think the issue is the extended dataset has Série A matches from a different season structure or includes additional rounds. For 2019, 81 matches in extended dataset means ~4.3 matches per team, which is weird.\n\nLet me check if the extended dataset dates for 2019 are valid Brasileirão dates. The 2019 season ran April-December. Some dates like 2019-11-28, 2019-11-14, 2019-10-11, 2019-09-26, 2019-06-13, 2019-04-28 look like real midweek match dates. But Brasileirao_Matches.csv might have those matches on different dates. Let me check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6ec5d5001zS2GLAQyLemBrn","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","messageID":"msg_efc6e83070010hvgcOMbzxxwG1"}}
