 in the main dataset. They might be from a different league year or mislabeled. For the purpose of this task, I think it's acceptable. The spec doesn't require exact real-world accuracy, just that the server can calculate standings from the provided data.\n\nHowever, to make the results more sensible, I could exclude the BR-Football-Dataset \"Brasileirão\" entries because they seem to be lower-quality duplicates. But the spec says all 6 CSV files must be queryable. They still are for Copa do Brasil etc.\n\nI think the current implementation is good enough. The tests pass, the build works, and sample queries produce reasonable results.\n\nLet me clean up and do a final verification. Let me also add a few more tests for the edge cases we fixed, like Atletico team distinction.\n\nActually, let me add a test that Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR are distinct.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6f2b09001KueP1s21VAt7Oo","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","messageID":"msg_efc6f0bfa001HZM2qWGib8zS8f"}}
