{"type":"text","timestamp":1782351694406,"sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","part":{"id":"prt_efc707874001lf56F6mpdTJmr8","messageID":"msg_efc7067860019i2OA83yPdhqFb","sessionID":"ses_1039ff0e7ffeYLNCCZGRmA53B2","type":"text","text":"Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server in TypeScript.\n\nCreated files:\n- `package.json` / `package-lock.json` — project config with MCP SDK, csv-parse, TypeScript, Vitest\n- `tsconfig.json` / `.gitignore` — TypeScript and ignore rules\n- `src/types.ts` — shared Match, Player, TeamStats, StandingRecord types\n- `src/normalize.ts` — team-name normalization, date parsing, UTF-8 handling\n- `src/data.ts` — loaders for all 6 CSV files in `data/kaggle/` plus cross-source deduplication\n- `src/query.ts` — query engine for matches, head-to-head, team stats, players, standings, top scorers, biggest wins, aggregate stats, and team rankings\n- `src/index.ts` — MCP server exposing 11 tools via stdio transport\n- `src/query.test.ts` — 21 BDD-style tests covering the spec’s success criteria\n\nVerified:\n- `npm run build` compiles cleanly\n- `npm test` passes (21/21 tests)\n- Server starts without errors\n\nSample outputs verified:\n- Flamengo vs Fluminense head-to-head\n- Palmeiras 2023 record\n- 2019 Brasileirão standings (calculated from matches)\n- Brazilian players by club/nationality","time":{"start":1782351689844,"end":1782351694404}}}
